<p>Use the following procedure to register a frequently used custom paper 
 size.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Up to ten custom paper sizes can be registered. 
 Depending on the printer you are using, up to 100 custom paper sizes can 
 be registered.</p></li>
<li><p>This setting cannot be selected from the printer 
 properties dialog box when opened from an application.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-OS">Devices and Printers</span> 
 window, open the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="2">
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Options</span> 
 tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Register Custom 
 Paper Size...</span> button to open the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>In <span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size List:</span>, 
 select an unused size or the size you want to change.</p></li>
<li><p>If necessary, in the <span class="Term-Soft">Name:</span> 
 box, change the name for this size using up to 24 characters.</p></li>
<li><p>Enter the length and width of the paper as seen 
 in the graphic.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">In <span class="Term-Soft">Width:</span>, 
 enter the size of the paper edge that is vertical relative to feed direction.</p></li>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">In <span class="Term-Soft">Length:</span>, 
 enter the size of the paper edge that is horizontal relative to feed direction.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="7">
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Modify</span> 
 button to update <span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size List:</span> 
 with information in the <span class="Term-Soft">Edit</span> area.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the 
 printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
